##gff-version 3
chr1	jb2hubs	sequence_alteration	2429109	2429336	.	.	.	ID=polled-celtic;Name=Celtic polled (Pc);Note=A 202 bp insertion-deletion: 212 bp duplicated in place of 10 bp. One copy stops horns growing%2C in Angus and many other European breeds%3B polled Holstein-Friesians carry a different allele. ARS-UCD1.2%2C a horned Hereford%2C lacks it.;in_panel=Angus alone;citation=Medugorac et al. 2012%2C PLoS One https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0039477,OMIA 000483-9913 https://omia.org/OMIA000483/9913/
chr13	jb2hubs	sequence_alteration	63639812	63648215	.	.	.	ID=asip-l1bt;Name=L1-BT at ASIP;Note=ARS-UCD1.2 carries a full-length L1-BT retrotransposon in ASIP's 5' region. An L1-BT inserted 5' of ASIP drives extra ASIP transcripts in Normande cattle and may cause their brindle coat (the Abr allele).;in_panel=Angus%2C Brahman and Highland carry it%3B the other eight assemblies lack it;citation=Girardot et al. 2006%2C Pigment Cell Res https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0749.2006.00312.x
chr6	jb2hubs	sequence_alteration	70052679	70052679	.	.	.	ID=kit-spotting;Name=KIT white-spotting deletion;Note=A 6.9 kb deletion 114 kb upstream of KIT causes the white spotting of Holstein-Friesian cattle. Herefords nearly all carry it%2C and so does ARS-UCD1.2%2C so an assembly drawn with an insertion here keeps the ancestral sequence%2C long (6.9 kb) or intermediate (6.0 kb).;in_panel=Angus%2C Nellore and Simmental share the deletion%3B Original Braunvieh and Piedmontese carry the intermediate allele%2C the other six the long one;citation=Jivanji et al. 2025%2C Sci Adv https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adt5913
chr6	jb2hubs	sequence_alteration	70099508	70120129	.	.	.	ID=kit-white-head;Name=KIT white-head duplication;Note=Tandem copies of a 14.3 kb repeat 66 kb upstream of KIT go with the white head of Hereford%2C Simmental and Fleckvieh cattle. ARS-UCD1.2 is a Hereford%2C but assembled fewer copies than Herefords carry.;in_panel=Simmental%2C the other white-headed breed%2C carries 17 kb more%3B the other ten assemblies 21 kb less;citation=Milia et al. 2025%2C Genome Res https://doi.org/10.1101/gr.279064.124
